WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.392
Welcome!

00:00:00.392 --> 00:00:05.880
In this video, we'll explain how to manage your handling times and fulfillment settings.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:09.980
There are four main settings that can affect order handling times.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:17.300
Default handling time, handling capacity, weekend operations, and asin-specific handling time.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:21.080
Each of these can make a big difference when it comes to making a sale.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.931
Why is handling time so important?

00:00:23.931 --> 00:00:26.800
It's a key part of earning customer trust.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.160
Every offer in the Amazon store comes with a customer delivery promise.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.340
This is the range of dates in which a customer can expect an order to arrive.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:42.205
The customer delivery promise consists of handling time, which is the number of days needed for

00:00:42.205 --> 00:00:44.120
you to prepare and ship orders.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.700
Transit time, which is the number of days your selected carrier needs to deliver packages.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:56.218
And occasionally, additional buffers to protect your delivery promise in case of carrier delivery

00:00:56.218 --> 00:00:58.080
issues or weather events.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:03.830
It's important that customers receive their orders before the final date of the customer delivery

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.180
promise.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:09.160
Products that arrive late make customers doubt if you can deliver on time.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:12.800
Late deliveries can also hurt your account health.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:19.647
If a customer sees two offers in the Amazon store that are the same price but have different customer

00:01:19.647 --> 00:01:20.300
delivery promises,

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:26.340
the offer with the shortest customer delivery promise will be more likely to win the featured offer.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:32.649
Since that's the one customers will be more likely to purchase, it's in your best interest to have

00:01:32.649 --> 00:01:34.560
the most accurate handling time possible.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:41.966
A 2019 study found that merchant fulfilled sellers in the US overestimate domestic handling times

00:01:41.966 --> 00:01:44.280
by an average of 53%.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:50.293
That means that their customer delivery promises are longer than they need to be, which makes for

00:01:50.293 --> 00:01:51.000
missed opportunities.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:57.282
The most basic way to improve your customer delivery promise is to shorten your default handling

00:01:57.282 --> 00:01:57.640
time.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:03.840
Depending on when you created your seller account, your default handling time was set to one or

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:04.480
two days.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:10.325
A one day handling time means that you'll ship an order by the end of the business day after it

00:02:10.325 --> 00:02:10.840
was received.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:15.080
While a two day handling time adds another business day.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:20.896
If you can prepare orders quickly, shortening your handling time will make your offers more appealing

00:02:20.896 --> 00:02:21.580
to customers.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:27.886
If you ship your orders out on the same day that you receive them, you may want to switch to same

00:02:27.886 --> 00:02:28.980
day default handling time.

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:35.698
Unlike one day handling time, same day handling time means that you'll ship orders on the same day

00:02:35.698 --> 00:02:36.360
they're received,

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:39.800
provided the order was placed before a set cutoff time.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:43.960
Note that same day handling time isn't the same as same day delivery.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.941
Same day delivery is part of premium shipping and means that customers will receive an order on

00:02:49.941 --> 00:02:51.500
the same day it's placed.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:56.880
Same day handling time means that you'll send an order out on the same day that it's placed,

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:01.140
provided that the order was received before a set cutoff time.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:03.771
The default cutoff time is 2 p.

00:03:03.771 --> 00:03:04.025
m.

00:03:04.025 --> 00:03:07.580
in your local time zone, but you can edit this to suit your needs.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:14.350
To change this time, hover over the gear icon in the upper right corner of Seller Central and click

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:15.280
Shipping Settings.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:21.724
On the Shipping Settings page, under the General Shipping Settings tab, locate the Order Fulfillment

00:03:21.724 --> 00:03:24.460
Settings section, then click the Edit button.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:30.580
On the Order Fulfillment Settings page, scroll down to the Carrier Specific Preferences section

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:34.780
and choose a time from one of the order cutoff time drop down menus.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:40.020
To set your default handling time, open the Settings menu in Seller Central.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:45.480
Select Shipping Settings and then choose General Shipping Settings on the next screen.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:48.700
Scroll down until you find Handling Time.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:54.780
If you haven't changed anything since creating your account, this will be set to one or two days.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:57.060
To the right, select Edit.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:00.740
You'll find an option for same day handling time here.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:08.200
Select the circle in front of same day under Choose Your Default Handling Time, then select Save.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:14.080
It may take up to 30 minutes for the new handling time to be reflected in your delivery promise.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:19.897
Because setting a new default handling time means adjusting the customer delivery promise for all

00:04:19.897 --> 00:04:24.940
of your ASINs, you can only change your handling time once every 24 hours.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:30.610
You may be worried that setting a short handling time could cause a problem if you receive a sudden

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:31.420
spike in orders.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:36.040
Sometimes you can see spikes coming, like around the holiday season.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:42.541
Other spikes may be unexpected, like if your brand suddenly becomes popular or a customer places

00:04:42.541 --> 00:04:43.640
a large order.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:50.144
Keeping the customer delivery promise is important, but you don't need to extend your default handling

00:04:50.144 --> 00:04:52.640
time to accommodate potential spikes in ordering.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:56.580
Instead, you can set your order handling capacity.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:03.278
Order handling capacity sets a limit on the number of orders you can fulfill within your default

00:05:03.278 --> 00:05:03.960
handling time.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:10.097
If you have a one-day default handling time and the number of orders you get exceeds your order

00:05:10.097 --> 00:05:16.180
handling capacity, Amazon will automatically add a day to the handling time and set all additional

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:18.720
orders to a two-day handling time.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:22.140
Note that these orders will count towards your next day's limit.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:30.214
So, if your order capacity is 100 orders and you get 120, the extra 20 are put toward the next day's

00:05:30.214 --> 00:05:30.960
order capacity.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:36.640
This way, you'll never have more orders than you can handle and you can protect your account health.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:42.040
You set your order handling capacity in the same place that you set your default handling time.

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:48.240
If you scroll down, you'll see order handling capacity right under default handling time.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.584
Here you set your capacity.

00:05:50.584 --> 00:05:52.460
Then select save below.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:58.827
Note that order handling capacity only affects non-prime orders with handling times between zero

00:05:58.827 --> 00:05:59.920
and two days.

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:06.891
If you've set a handling time greater than two days for a specific ASIN, orders for that ASIN won't

00:06:06.891 --> 00:06:08.620
count towards your handling capacity.

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:14.780
Weekends and holidays normally count as non-business days in the customer delivery promise.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:21.455
So, if your handling time is normally two days and someone purchases your product on a Monday, you'll

00:06:21.455 --> 00:06:23.540
be expected to ship by Wednesday.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:29.348
In addition, Saturday and Sunday won't count towards your handling time for a product purchased

00:06:29.348 --> 00:06:32.780
on Friday, which you'll be expected to ship on Tuesday.

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:38.762
If you're able to ship products on the weekend, however, you can make your listings more appealing

00:06:38.762 --> 00:06:40.520
to customers by enabling weekend operations.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:44.735
You can do so on the order fulfillment settings page.

00:06:44.735 --> 00:06:51.148
Scroll down to account level preferences or select it from the menu on the left to edit your settings

00:06:51.148 --> 00:06:52.160
for weekend operations.

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:58.238
Here, you can choose to have your packages picked up by shipping providers on Saturday, Sunday,

00:06:58.238 --> 00:06:58.900
or both.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:06.071
You may have enabled shipping settings automation or SSA using your shipping templates to automatically

00:07:06.071 --> 00:07:07.860
calculate your delivery promise.

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:15.121
If so, you'll also need to enable weekend operations for SSA-enabled products in the carrier specific

00:07:15.121 --> 00:07:19.880
preferences section, which can be found on the order fulfillment settings page.

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:23.880
Note that you won't set a cutoff time for SSA.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:24.900
That's calculated automatically.

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:31.466
For more information on SSA, search for shipping settings automation in Seller University or in

00:07:31.466 --> 00:07:32.240
Seller Central.

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:38.079
Once you've chosen your desired settings, don't forget to save them using the button in the upper

00:07:38.079 --> 00:07:38.380
right.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:44.254
That covers how to set handling settings that affect your whole catalog, which will help you offer

00:07:44.254 --> 00:07:45.740
a better customer delivery promise.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:51.001
But what if you want to set a short default handling time, but some of the ASINs in your catalog

00:07:51.001 --> 00:07:53.520
are hard to get out of the door in one day?

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:57.640
Setting ASIN specific handling times can be the solution.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:03.320
If you have a product that you can ship out faster than your default time or one that needs more

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:09.744
time than normal, you can use an ASIN specific handling time to give customers more accurate delivery

00:08:09.744 --> 00:08:10.120
promises.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:17.071
As an example, if you've set a same-day default handling time, but one particularly delicate product

00:08:17.071 --> 00:08:23.898
needs special prep before it gets shipped out, you could set that ASIN to a two-day handling time

00:08:23.898 --> 00:08:26.340
while still delivering your other products swiftly.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:33.266
Because ASIN specific handling times need to be set separately for each ASIN, you don't set them

00:08:33.266 --> 00:08:34.980
from the shipping settings page.

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:39.500
Instead, you'll find these settings on the Manage Inventory page.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:45.780
To get there, open the main menu in Seller Central by clicking the menu icon in the upper left corner.

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:50.340
Hover over Inventory, then select Manage All Inventory.

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:55.280
Select the checkbox next to the ASIN in your inventory that you want to modify.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:59.480
Then select the Edit button at the far right end of that row.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:04.700
Depending on the size of your screen, you may have to scroll to the right to find that button.

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:09.740
On the next page, select the Offer tab and then scroll down to Handling Time.

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:16.780
You can set the handling time here in Business Days, so if you enter two, it means that you'll have

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:22.826
two business days after receiving an order for that ASIN in which to both ship the product and confirm

00:09:22.826 --> 00:09:24.440
the shipment in Seller Central.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:31.753
While you'll normally need to set ASIN specific handling times for ASINs one by one, you can upload

00:09:31.753 --> 00:09:36.940
a file to set handling times in bulk if you're familiar with the Inventory Loader tool.

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:42.520
Search for "Modify" handling time in Seller Central to learn more about this option.

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:49.459
Handling time is a key part of the customer delivery promise and your account health, so it's important

00:09:49.459 --> 00:09:53.340
to have an accurate handling time for each product you sell.

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:59.495
Remember, having an accurate customer delivery promise is an important part of being a successful

00:09:59.495 --> 00:09:59.860
seller.

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:06.400
Customers prefer offers with shorter delivery times, so it's important for your business to have

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:08.280
the best handling time possible.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:12.020
That begins with setting the right default handling time.

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:18.815
You can set order handling capacity, cutoff time, and weekend operations to improve this setting

00:10:18.815 --> 00:10:20.860
while protecting your account health.

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:27.389
For ASINs that require special care, you can set ASIN specific handling times while still keeping

00:10:27.389 --> 00:10:31.120
your default handling times for the rest of your catalog.

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:37.140
This can help you delight customers and maximize your performance in the Amazon Store.

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:41.540
This concludes our training on handling times and fulfillment settings.

00:10:42.020 --> 00:10:42.560
Thank you.
